  "pr_title": "build(tooling): publish a GitHub release for each version tag",
  "pr_description": "## Goal\n\nEach pushed `vX.Y.Z` tag publishes a GitHub release with the standalone CLI, its checksum, and the plugin files. Teammates and BRAT then install tested versions, and the plugin can download the CLI build for its own version.\n\n## Summary\n\n`.github/workflows/release.yml` runs on `v*.*.*` tags on a `macos-15` runner, which is Apple silicon. Before the build, the workflow checks that the tag matches the three manifests, and it reads the release notes from `CHANGELOG.md`. A wrong tag or a missing changelog section stops the workflow before anything is published. The workflow then builds the plugin and the standalone CLI. It publishes these release files:\n\n- `spsync-macos-arm64.tar.gz`\n- `spsync-macos-arm64.tar.gz.sha256`, one line in `shasum -a 256` format\n- `main.js` and `manifest.json`, the names that BRAT reads\n- `spsync-X.Y.Z-source.tar.gz`, the complete corresponding source code of the CLI build\n\nThe CLI archive bundles merge3, which is licensed under GPL-2.0-or-later, and other dependencies under permissive licenses. GPLv2 section 3(a) lets a binary ship together with its complete corresponding source code, so the release needs no written offer. `scripts/source_archive.py` writes the source archive. It holds the spsync source at the tag, from `git archive`, and the source distribution of each bundled package. The script downloads each source distribution from the URL in `uv.lock` and stops when the SHA-256 hash differs from the lock. `scripts/bundle_licenses.py` adds `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` and a `licenses/` folder to the CLI archive. The notices list each bundled package, its version, its license, and a source link, and they name the source archive. The script reads the package list from `uv export`, so the notices follow `uv.lock`. The build fails when a bundled package has no license file. `pyproject.toml` gains a `Repository` URL, which the notices use to link to the source at the tag.\n\n`build_standalone.sh` now keeps the spsync package metadata in the Nuitka build. Without the metadata, `spsync --version` and `spsync doctor` printed \"unknown\" in the standalone build. The script also stops when the version of the built executable differs from the manifests.\n\n`scripts/release_notes.py` prints the changelog section of one version. `CHANGELOG.md` follows Keep a Changelog, with the current features under Unreleased. `RELEASING.md` describes the release steps:\n\n- the version bump\n- `uv lock`\n- the changelog update\n- the tag\n- the verification\n- the recovery from a failed workflow\n- the test release\n- the code signing limits\n\nThe README License section describes the notices in the archive. The change does not touch docx reading or patching.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `tests/test_bundle_licenses.py` runs the script on merge3 and httpx. It checks the copied license files, the GPL row, the source archive name, and the skip of a package that is not installed. It also checks that permissive packages get no source section.\n- `tests/test_source_archive.py` builds a source archive from a temporary repository and a local source distribution. It checks the archive layout, a hash mismatch, and a package without a locked source distribution. The tests remove the `GIT_*` variables from the environment, so the pre-commit hook does not leak its repository into the temporary one.\n- `tests/test_release_notes.py` checks the extraction of one section, the stop at the link definitions, and the failure for a missing or empty section.\n- `actionlint` 1.7.12 reports no findings for the workflow.\n- Manual check: `scripts/build_standalone.sh` built the archive on an Apple silicon Mac. The archive contains `LICENSE`, `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`, and license files for 20 packages and Python. The extracted `spsync --version` prints `spsync 0.1.0`, and `spsync doctor --json` runs. `scripts/source_archive.py` wrote a 13 MB source archive with the spsync source and 20 source distributions.\n- Not yet run: a pushed test tag. After this PR merges, a `v0.0.1` test tag from a throwaway branch checks the complete release. Then the test release, the tag, and the branch are deleted.\n- `uv run ruff format --check`, `uv run ruff check`, `uv run ty check`, `uv run anti-slop-python src tests scripts`, and `uv run pytest` pass.\n\n## Issue\n\nCloses #11\n"
